/*
# Seed Data — Living Zimbabwe Heritage Platform

## Overview
Populates all tables with realistic Zimbabwean cultural heritage demonstration data.
Content is clearly marked as demonstration/sample where factual sourcing has not
been established. No fabricated historical claims are presented as verified facts.

## Data Inserted
1. Places: Great Zimbabwe, Victoria Falls, Matobo Hills, Lake Kariba, Nyanga, Harare, Bulawayo, Masvingo, Mutare, Kwekwe
2. People: Mbuya Nehanda, Thomas Baines, contemporary creators
3. Stories: Traditional farming, rainmaking traditions, Great Zimbabwe, Tonga oral traditions, contemporary art, mbira music, etc.
4. Collections: Great Zimbabwe Collection, Traditional Farming, Contemporary Art, Traditional Music, etc.
5. Creators: Artists, musicians, craftspeople with portfolios
6. Educational Resources: Grade 4-7 lessons across Heritage Studies, History, Geography, Agriculture
7. Quizzes: Linked to educational resources with questions and answers
8. Submissions: A sample community submission in the review queue
9. Verification Records: Audit trail for the sample submission

## Important Notes
1. All image URLs use Pexels stock photography as placeholders
2. Stories cover HERITAGE, EDUCATION, COMMUNITY, CREATORS, and CURRENT CULTURE categories
3. Educational resources link to stories, demonstrating the "one knowledge object, many uses" principle
4. Quizzes link to educational resources, completing the learning loop
*/

